Every item in your project has a scratchpad: a page of notes kept beside its text. Use it for
what the text still needs, such as a question to settle, a fact to check or a list of changes
for the next draft.

## Notes that stay private

The scratchpad belongs to you, not to the book.

- It is never exported.
- It never counts towards your words, your targets or your pace.
- Searching the project does not look in it.

It is saved with the project and kept in every backup, like the rest of your writing.

## Opening the scratchpad

The *Scratchpad* panel is on the right of the window. Open it with its icon, a spiral pad, or
with `Ctrl+Shift+A`. *View ▸ Panels* lists it too.

Write in it as in any text: bold, lists and links work the same way. Its font and text size
are your own choice, in *Settings ▸ Editor ▸ Typography ▸ Scratchpad*.

## Which item it shows

The panel shows the scratchpad of the item in front of you, and the line at its top names
that item.

- In a scene, a note or any other item open in a tab, it is that item's scratchpad.
- In the full text of a chapter, a part or a book, it follows the scene your cursor is in.
  When you click into the scratchpad to write, it stays on that scene.
- On a chapter's own page, its corkboard or its overview, it is the chapter's scratchpad.

While the project is open, each scratchpad remembers where you left the cursor.

## Items in the trash

An item in the trash keeps its scratchpad. You can read it, but you cannot change it until
you restore the item.

## Merging, splitting and duplicating

- *Merge with previous* joins the two scratchpads. The notes of the scene you merge are added
  after the notes of the scene before it.
- *Split scene* leaves the scratchpad with the first scene. The new scene starts with an empty
  one.
- *Duplicate* copies the scratchpad with the item.

## Earlier versions

The project keeps the scratchpad's earlier versions, as it does for your text. To see them,
open the *Versions* panel and choose *Scratchpad* at its top. *Restore this version* puts one
back, and `Ctrl+Z` in the scratchpad undoes that. See
[Backups and versions](:help-backups-and-versions).

## Items without a scratchpad

The *End of Book* marker, and the other markers that hold no text, have no scratchpad. The
panel says so when one of them is in front of you.
